In the provided code snippet, the cleanup functions are set up immediately after memory allocation, which is before the actual resource initialization (reading from I/O). If an error occurs during memory allocation, the cleanup functions will be set but the resources will not be fully initialized, potentially leading to a use-after-free vulnerability.

